---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const canonical = new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who I am, what I work on, and how to reach me."
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <article>
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>
    <p>
      I'm Josip Ravas, DevOps &amp; Architecture Lead at{' '}
      <a href="https://prototyp.digital">Prototyp</a>. I work on infrastructure, CI/CD, and the part
      that comes after shipping a control: proving it fires. A rule set left in count mode, an alert
      rule querying a metric nothing writes, a test suite no job runs. Each of those is configured
      correctly by every visible signal and protects nothing, and the only signal you get is a green
      one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of what I write here comes out of running production systems for a European automotive
      client, and out of measuring my own work rather than trusting my impression of it. I also
      wrote and maintain{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/prototypdigital/bluetemberg">Bluetemberg</a>, which ships AI
      coding standards as signed, version-locked npm packages.
    </p>
    <p>
      The essays here are the primary versions. When a piece is cross-posted elsewhere, the
      cross-post carries a canonical link back to this site.
    </p>
    <ul class="chips">
      <li><a href="mailto:ping@jravas.dev">ping@jravas.dev</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/josip-ravas-2a7769110/">linkedin →</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/jravas">github →</a></li>
      <li><a href="/rss.xml">rss →</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
